Array Big O
1. push and pop at the end of array means no reindexing requires so iteration so it will be o(1)
2.shift, unshift means adding and removing at first location of array requires reindexing and that means
  iteration of array so it will be O(n)
3. in case of splice, where we have to add or remove at any place of array in that case we need reindexing and iteration so 
  it will be O(n)
4. if search by number then O(n)
5. if search by index then O(1)
